From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: EglantinePS5 <noreply@eglantineps5.local>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 08:40:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] vulkan: EDEN_GPU_TIME=1 turns on the GPU time probe in any build

Core patch, after 0263. Off unless the switch is set.

No build measures how busy the GPU is. The probe exists (headless/gpu_time_probe.inc), but only dev-settings
gpu_time=on sets its flag, and that is read in EDEN_DEV_PROFILE builds, as is the MKW diagnostic build's line.

Its natural place is beside EDEN_PERF_REPORT in headless/main.cpp, but this series only reaches the Eglantine
tree, and a patch for headless/ would stop the build. So it sits in the scheduler's constructor, before the
first command buffer and the worker thread.

vk_scheduler.cpp as it stands doesn't include dev_vulkan.h. The port adds it, and headless/vulkan.cmake always
builds the port's vulkan_scheduler.cpp instead. If that changes, this stops compiling.

Every 5 s the probe prints "EDEN_GPU_TIME wall_ms= busy_ms= submissions= max_ms=" to stdout, which is heap.log.
Busy share is busy_ms / wall_ms. It costs two timestamps a submission, not measured on these builds.

Compiled with the build's flags from the port's output, syntax only. Not linked, not run.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
diff --git a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_scheduler.cpp b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_scheduler.cpp
index 6c4d9a0..5ea2fa2 100644
--- a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_scheduler.cpp
+++ b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_scheduler.cpp
@@ -58,6 +58,11 @@ Scheduler::Scheduler(const Device& device_, StateTracker& state_tracker_)
     : device{device_}, state_tracker{state_tracker_},
       master_semaphore{std::make_unique<MasterSemaphore>(device)},
       command_pool{std::make_unique<CommandPool>(*master_semaphore, device)} {
+    // EDEN_GPU_TIME=1: the probe of gpu_time_probe.inc, in any build. dev-settings gpu_time=on is
+    // read in development profile builds only. Before the first command buffer on purpose.
+    if (const char* const value = std::getenv("EDEN_GPU_TIME"); value != nullptr && value[0] == '1') {
+        ::Eden::DevVulkan::gpu_time = true;
+    }
     if (const char* const value = std::getenv("EDEN_NX2_HANG_WATCH");
         value != nullptr && value[0] != '0') {
         hang_watching = true;
